From e292c43b5d8998edd833cfd9196fb6d328e44abf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 03:51:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ask: FMAN/DPAA EHASH foundation for fast-path offload
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The foundation patch for the ASK fast-path stack on LS1046A.

Brings in the NXP FMAN/DPAA vendor driver (drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/
sdk_dpaa, sdk_fman, drivers/staging/fsl_qbman) with ASK-specific
EHASH extensions for hardware packet classification, declares
the master CONFIG_CPE_FAST_PATH Kconfig in net/Kconfig, and extends the
core kernel with the skb fields (abm_ff, expt_pkt, iif_index,
underlying_iif/vlan_tci, qosmark, ipsec_offload, ipsec_xfrm_dir) and
netdevice/net_device fields (wifi_offload_dev) plus the dev_queue_xmit
hook infrastructure (dpaa_wifi_xmit_local_ipsec_handler,
dpa_register_wifi_xmit_local_hook, original_dev_queue_xmit,
dpa_add_dummy_eth_hdr) that downstream slices (020-080) consume.

Every cdx-registered hook has a matching unregister
(dpa_unregister_ipsec_fq_handler, dpa_unregister_ceetm_get_egress_fq,
dpa_unregister_wifi_xmit_local_hook) that clears the pointer and
synchronize_rcu()s before returning, so cdx deinit — including the
failed-init unwind — can free module text safely and a later load can
register again. Datapath readers take a READ_ONCE snapshot instead of
re-reading the global across the NULL check and the call.

Also ships the NETLINK_FF=30, NETLINK_KEY=32, NETLINK_L2FLOW=33 protocol
reservations in UAPI.

Compiles warning-free: cross-TU APIs are declared in their owning
headers (fm_ehash.h, fm_cc.h, fm_kg.h, fm_port_ext.h, fsl_fman_port.h,
fm_muram_ext.h, lnxwrp_fsl_fman.h, dpaa_eth.h), single-TU helpers are
static, and the stray format specifiers / unused locals are fixed.

Roll back completed port PCD bindings on partial setup failures. Publish
classification-plan groups only after allocation and count port owners
only after a successful bind, preserving shared groups on failed setup.

Keep port PCD ownership until public API cleanup completes, including
parser statistics and the environment reference.
Balance locks on setup failures and preserve unfinished cleanup for retry;
check MURAM-page allocation and unwind partial frame-engine support.

Retain the charged dequeue depth beyond port initialization and release
FM port resources only after successful acquisition, once per lifetime.

Disable unsupported whole-tree replacement while retaining the SDK API
and native/compat ioctl numbers. Reject requests before accessing their
arguments or classifier state and remove the unused compat converter.

Remove unsupported IP/CAPWAP hardware reassembly and the old ASK
external-hash reassembly tables. Reserve public identifiers/layouts and
reject requests before allocations or cookie lookup. Keep absent-table
sentinels in normal microcode descriptors.

Validate complete FM port resource requests before committing hardware
and shared accounting. Serialize resource updates and leave rejected
initialization or resize requests unchanged, with interrupts restored.

Commit keygen scheme deletion only after successful hardware deletion.
Keep required actions, netenv ownership and the scheme lock on refusal
or command failure, and return the lock once after a successful retry.

Translate the public keygen direct-scheme flag to the SDK layout and
reject ordinary schemes without a network environment. Preserve the
native and compat ioctl layouts and return compat next-engine data.

Track HC buffer ownership through enqueue rejection, completion and
timeout. Quarantine accepted unconfirmed frames and latch timeout failure
until board reset; keep QMan acceptance separate from SDK completion.

Build KG scheme changes in a private candidate, publish only after
successful programming, and balance failed lock acquisitions. Preserve
existing scheme ownership on failure and transfer netenv references on commit.

Copy the layout-checked scheme tail through its containing objects so
FORTIFY retains the full source and destination bounds. Bound compat
union copies by the source member and reject reserved reassembly conversion.

Signed-off-by: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
